            <ArticleTitle>Surgical treatment of chronic pancreatitis: an overview.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>661-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The correct management of chronic pancreatitis remains undecided. The aims of surgical treatment are to relieve pain, treat complications and preserve pancreatic function. The appropriate surgical procedure to achieve these ends must be carefully chosen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
